# Implementation Plan — Premium New UI Components & Screens

This implementation plan details the addition of the new UI components and screens outlined in the style guide file. The designs showcase soft-morphism, custom interactive controls, Nunito-based typography, and gorgeous layout grids that elevate the HelperHive application to a premium state.

We will build these layouts as highly modular, reusable components so they can be easily maintained and plugged into any part of the application. To allow full testing, we will integrate them into a dedicated navigation wrapper ("New UI Mode") accessible via the home page dashboard toggle.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Key Integration & Theme Coexistence:** 
> We are adding new color tokens (`primaryPink`, `secondaryGreen`, `accentYellow`, `skyBlue`, `alertOrange`) and a new typography set (`Nunito`) alongside the existing green brand colors and Midnight theme. To achieve this cleanly without breaking existing client or provider screens:
> 1. We will merge the new color palette directly into [app_colors.dart](file:///c:/Users/lenovo/Desktop/google/sync_app/lib/core/theme/app_colors.dart) as secondary accent colors.
> 2. We will create dedicated, reusable widgets under `lib/widgets/new_ui/` that use these colors and apply the `Nunito` Google Font explicitly.
> 3. We will register a new navigation flow so you can toggle between the **Classic Green UI**, the **AI Search Dashboard**, and this **New Soft-UI Design System** with one click.

